<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila needs to import 1.0 mln T corn in '98-trade.</title>
<headline>Manila needs to import 1.0 mln T corn in '98-trade.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines needs to import about one million tonnes of corn in 1998 due to a projected production shortfall because of the El Nino weather phenomenon, an industry executive said on Friday.</p>
<p>Philippine Association of Hog Raisers Inc president Soledad Agbayani told reporters at an El Nino forum that a forecast of drought in some countries in Asia-Pacific would drive up prices of corn, wheat and soybean.</p>
<p>&quot;Corn-producing countries, including the United Sstates, would hoard for their own needs,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>Corn prices in the world market are currently pegged at an average of $140 per tonne, she said.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8936, Fax 817-6267</p>
</text>
